  "term": "spherical aberration",
  "definition": "Spherical aberration is a major higher-order optical imperfection in the human eye. It refers to a mismatch in the eye’s optical system that affects retinal image quality, normally moderated in youth by a balance between the cornea and crystalline lens, but tending to worsen with age as that balance is lost.",
